## Brief comparison to nanoGPT (see docs/experiments_golden_mean.md)
- nanoGPT (AR-only) GM: NLL ≈ 0.674 bits; p(0|0) ≈ 0.000; p(0|1) ≈ 0.498
- nanoGPT + aux state head: behavior preserved; pre-state linear decodability improves substantially
- EBM (this run) GM: ≈ 0.656 bits; p(0|0) ≈ 0.004; p(0|1) ≈ 0.553; representation plots show two regimes aligning with GM states

## Notes / Next
- For Even Process: increase context window (128–256), keep dropout=0.0; consider longer training for sharper parity separation.
- Optional: add an auxiliary parity loss for EBM if parity decodability is a target.

